indicate reference quantities used to non-dimensionalize 
the field quantities. Dimensional field quantities are denoted by a tilde. In a symbolic representation, the number of underlines indicates the tensorial order, e.g.,~$\underline{\tilde x}$ for the position vector and $\underline \nabla$ for the non-dimensional spatial derivative vector. Spatial vectors and tensors are usually defined with reference to Cartesian coordinates.
