\section{EXPERIMENTS}
Without loss of generality, we use HAM10000 \cite{33} to verify the effectiveness of the different algorithms. Without losing fairness, we chose to use RDP account for all the algorithm to test the effectiveness of the setting of different decay parameters. The implementation is available on \href{https://github.com/FangXieLab/SAD-DPSGD}{GitHub}. HAM10000 \cite{33} is a imbalanced dataset dominated by one major class: Melanocytic Nevi (NV),and consists of 10,015 dermatoscopic images categorized into seven classes labeled from 0 to 6, including Actinic keratoses (AK), Basal cell carcinoma (BCC), Benign keratosis-like lesions (BKL), Dermatofibroma (DF), Melanocytic nevi (NV), Vascular lesions (VASC), and Melanoma (MEL). The distribution of the overall dataset is presented as follows in Figure \hyperref[fig2]{2}.
