We further propose a \textbf{M}ulti-Scale and \textbf{M}ulti-Level \textbf{M}emory \textbf{F}ailure \textbf{P}rediction framework (M$^2$-MFP). The framework introduces a novel Multi-Level Binary Spatial Feature Extractor (Multi-BSFE) to derive representations of potential failure characteristics from CEs. Subsequently, M$^2$-MFP integrates a dual-path temporal modeling architecture comprising a \emph{Time-Patch Scale Prediction Module} for capturing local event patterns across temporal windows and a \emph{Time-Point Scale Prediction Module} for identifying crucial failure-inducing events at specific time points. This dual channel predictor demonstrates adaptability to predictions concerning both batch and streaming event sequence data. Compared to existing solutions, M$^2$-MFP exhibits enhanced intelligence, automation, and generalizability, necessitating minimal expert knowledge while significantly surpassing baselines in performance.

