The active learning process begins with an initial experimental design of 20 points generated via LHS. At each iteration, following the procedure described in \cref{sec_local_error_measures_for_SPCE}, 100 SPCE realizations are drawn to compute local error estimates. The failure probability associated with the emulator $\hat{P}_f$ is estimated using \cref{eq_Pf_random_variable_POV} with MCS of size $N_{\text{MCS}} = 10^5$ samples. To reduce the noise effects in the convergence curves, the $\hat{P}_f$  estimates are smoothed using a moving average filter over three iterations (see \cref{eq_smoothed_Pf}). A candidate set of $10^3$ points is used, and 5 points are added to the experimental design at each iteration until a total of $1{,}000$ samples is reached. During training, the SPCE settings include degree adaptivity with polynomial orders in $p \in [1, 4]$, and the latent variable is modeled as Gaussian.

