    \begin{claimproof}
        Consider $t \in V(T)$.
        For each $i \in \ccal$ with $\log(i) = t$, we compute all distances from $c_i$ in $G[V_t]$ using the linear single-source shortest path algorithm for $K_h$-minor-free graphs~\cite{TazariM09}.
        %Since $G[V_i]$ is $K$-minor-free, the number of its edges is $\Oh_K(|V_t|)$ and this bounds the running time of a single SSSP call.
