\smallskip
\noindent
\textbf{Baseline.}
\textit{Baseline} consists of a non-CHERI full-network stack. In this configuration, DPDK, F-Stack, and \iperf run on two different processes (comparison with Scenario~1), and as a single process (Scenario~2). This setup represents a system that uses the MMU to isolate the two processes, which limits the ability to achieve fine-grained isolation. % and, as noted in the introduction, is not always available in low-end embedded systems.

