This work has presented the potential of CHERI to provide strong security properties through compartmentalization of the software components of a network stack.
Specifically, we presented different trade-offs for designs that isolate DPDK, F-Stack, and a network benchmark application using Intravisor-based \cvm{s}.
Our evaluation on the CHERI-enabled Arm Morello platform has validated the effectiveness of CHERI compartmentalization and has shown the low overhead potential of our \cvm{}-based design.
However, despite achieving full bandwidth, the evaluation also underlined the impact of synchronization among different \cvm{s}.

% With this work, we have laid the groundwork for a complete CHERI compartmentalized network stacks, which can benefit future CHERI-enabled microcontrollers.
