	\begin{abstract}
		In connection to the Fuglede conjecture, and to Fuglede's original work \cite{Fug74}, 
	we study one-parameter unitary groups associated to self-adjoint extensions of the differential operator $Df=\frac1{2\pi i}f'$ on a union of finite intervals. We present a formula for such unitary groups and we use it to discover some geometric properties of such sets in $\br$ which admit orthogonal bases of exponential functions (also called spectral sets). 


